  speakerName: VENDOR IRAH
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Be careful around these delicate threads.

    If you accidentally
    bump into someone or make a mistake, you can apologize.

    In Ilokano, ''pakawanen
    nak'' means ''I am sorry.''

    Use it when you want to apologize for something
    you''ve done.

    Listen carefully: pakawanen nak.

    Now, try saying ''pakawanen
    nak'' yourself."

'
